  "reason": "the r10 head registers every host input at the pin (p_* pin flops, 2-flop reset sync) and every output is a leaf output register or a head status register; a kit flop stage would add an edge to the priced r7c schedule (D=4)"
 },
 "structural_change": "r10 parent (SFU-PS-2 10-17): 11 identical one-stripe leaves (hbm_sfu_store_stripe_r10_1017) + the thin head in ONE cluster, 3 cols x 4 rows with the head in the centre cell (c1,r1) so every leaf<->head leg is <= ~1 col + 1.5 rows. Rows (S->N): P2 P1 P0 | P6 head IO2 | P7 IO0 IO1(MY) | P5 P4 P3; config chains are neighbour hops (P0>P1>P2 and P3>P4>P5 westward in a row, P6>P7 and IO1>IO2 vertical, IO0>IO1 with IO1 mirrored so out/in halves face). Outputs (io_word 471 + compiler_control 1,742 + status) leave on the S face toward sfucore (2.4 pins/um), host config/start on the E face beside the head row, clock on the S face. Square-ish (0.94 x 0.95 mm) instead of 4x3 (1.23 x 0.69) to shrink the head radius (see lanes/SFU-PS-FUND.md: cross-leaf agreement paths).",
